    "aif-template": { g: "nvidia", t: "NVIDIA-Omniverse/aif-pipeline-samples — GB300 rack template + Vertiv XDU1350 metadata (MIT)",
      d: "NVIDIA-authored asset metadata, auto-generated from GB300_RACK.csv: 136 kW nameplate, EDPP2 240 kW / EDPP1 204 kW, 116 kW liquid / 19.3 kW air (87% capture), required-flow curve 65.1->160 LPM over 25->45 C, dP = 0.0048x^2 + 0.0617x kPa, idle 40.8 kW, ramp 20 W/s/GPU, 90%-floor smoothing 122.4 kW; XDU1350: 1,368 kW nominal, 3 pumps N+1, 13.7/20.5 kW pump power, 480 V, 650 kg, DN100. Repo at commit 4103896 (v1.0.0). Reconciliation note: the template's thermal rows do not close exactly as published — 116 liquid + 19.3 air = 135.3 kW vs the 136 kW nameplate, and 116/135.3 = 85.7% vs the stated \"87% capture\". All three values are carried faithfully (the discord is upstream, in the verify queue); plant sizing uses the explicit 116 kW-liquid figure x racks wherever a rack count exists; the cooling page's generic IT-block default uses the 87% headline capture ratio (1.3pp above the 85.7% split — its own note says so), and a platform pick seeds the reconciled 85.7. Density reading used by the capex page: 136 kW / 72 GPUs = 1.889 kW/GPU = 529 GPUs/MW — the GB300-template envelope; GB200 actuals are <= it (public 120-140 kW GB200 quotes lack an NVIDIA doc).",
      u: "https://github.com/NVIDIA-Omniverse/aif-pipeline-samples", a: "2026-08-22" },
